Structure dispatch (verbatim from docstring lines 71-75): P present (with or without F) → olivine Pnma; TM count sum = 2 (M2O4-type) → spinel Fd-3m; else → layered R-3m. For non-layered non-olivine: default layered (the "其余（默认）→ 层状 R-3m" branch); no rejection of non-layered compositions — e.g., Li2MnO3 (Li-rich, has Mn TM count 1) would go layered too. Note: build_doped_structure raises ValueError if no TM species or TM fractions don't sum to 1 (layered path only — _tm_fractions). In olivine/spinel paths, TM fractions are normalized.

Note the important nuance: P-containing compositions with F (fluorophosphates like Li2NiPO4F) are treated as olivine (docstring: "含 F 的氟盐类同近似，如实标注").

Voltage formula: V = −[E(Li_x2) − E(Li_x1) − n_removed·E_Li] / n_removed, with _X_FULL=1.0, _X_DELITH=0.3, seed from sha256 of formula. Capacity: capacity_mah_g = (1.0 − 0.3) * _F / mw where _F = 26801.481. Stability: rel_stability_ev_atom = e_full/n_atoms − base_energy_fu/4.0 (baseline NMC811 per-f.u. energy divided by 4 atoms/f.u.).

Also — did the parent ask about "what happens for non-layered non-olivine compositions"? Answer: default → layered R-3m prototype path (docstring: "其余（默认）→ 层状 R-3m（原有路径，完全不变）"). Only P-containing → olivine; TM sum = 2 → spinel. Also note: olivine builder excludes Li, O, P, Si, F from TM set; spinel excludes only Li, O.

