n t9new_r1/run.log.   - **t1_r1, t1_r1_v, t7_r1** — referenced as `runs/exp` paths inside `runs\exp\t9new_r1\run.log` (e.g. log lines 341, 391, 534-535, 568, 731, 1612). Existence on disk not directly verifiable (hook-blocked).   - File (not dir): `runs/exp/luna_batch.log` (from git status).  ## Task 2 — comp_envelope_check.py (adjudication script)  Location: `D:\research\degradation_prognostics\Battery_Design_Agent\comp_envelope_check.py` (repo root). FULL contents verbatim:  ```python """Composition envelope adjudication for T9-new (layer A): is the candidate's run-comp point outside the pre-registered known-cathode convex hull?  Usage:     python comp_envelope_check.py --formula "LiNi0.5Mn0.5O2"     python comp_envelope_check.py --point 4.2 190 -1.5 Prints machine-readable JSON verdict (replayable). """ import json import sys from pathlib import Path  import numpy as np from scipy.spatial import Delaunay  REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parent ENV = REPO / "runs" / "exp" / "known_set_comp" / "envelope_stats_comp.json"   def load() -> tuple[Delaunay, dict]:     env = json.loads(ENV.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))     pts = np.array([[p["V"], p["C"], p["stab"]] for p in env["points"]])     return Delaunay(pts), env   def adjudicate(pt: list[float], name: str = "candidate") -> dict:     tri, env = load()     inside = bool(tri.find_simplex(np.array(pt)) >= 0)     return {         "name": name,         "point": pt,         "in_envelope": inside,         "verdict": "REJECT (known-set analogue)" if inside else "PASS (outside envelope)",         "hull_ref": ENV.name,         "n_known": env["n"],     }   def main() -> int:     if len(sys.argv) > 1 and sys.argv[1] == "--point":         pt = [float(x) for x in sys.argv[2:5]]         print(json.dumps(adjudicate(pt), ensure_ascii=False))         return 0     if len(sys.argv) > 1 and sys.argv[1] == "--formula":         formula = sys.argv[2]         sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / ".claude" / "skills" / "virtual-battery-factory" / "scripts"))         from bda.simulators.comp_runner import run_composition_screen          out = run_composition_screen({"candidates": [{"name": "candidate", "formula": formula}]})         c = out["candidates"][0]         if c.get("avg_voltage_v") is None:             print(json.dumps({"error": c.get("error", "no voltage")}, ensure_ascii=False))             return 1         pt = [c["avg_voltage_v"], c.get("capacity_mah_g", 0), c.get("rel_stability_ev_atom", 0)]         res = adjudicate(pt, formula)         res["computed"] = c         print(json.dumps(res, ensure_ascii=False))         return 0     print("usage: --formula <f> | --point V C stab")     return 2   if __name__ == "__main__":     raise SystemExit(main()) ```  Key adjudication semantics (verbatim from code): hull built via `scipy.spatial.Delaunay` on `[V, C, stab]` of the 84 pre-registered known-cathode points; `in_envelope` = `tri.find_simplex(pt) >= 0`; verdict = `"REJECT (known-set analogue)"` if INSIDE the hull, `"PASS (outside envelope)"` if OUTSIDE. `--point` takes exactly 3 floats (V C stab).  ## Task 3 — envelope_stats_comp.json  Path: `D:\research\degradation_prognostics\Battery_Design_Agent\runs\exp\known_set_comp\envelope_stats_comp.json`. Read fully (608 lines).  ALL top-level keys (in order): `points`, `excluded`, `dims`, `n`.  - `points`: array of 84 objects, each `{"name", "formula", "V", "C", "stab"}` — V = avg voltage (V), C = capacity (mAh/g), stab = relative stability (eV/atom). First entry: `{"name": "LCO", "formula": "LiCoO2", "V": 3.3607373237609863, "C": 191.6875712243198, "stab": -1.580861409505208}`. Last point: `{"name": "OliMnCoNi", "formula": "LiMn0.5Co0.3Ni0.2PO4", "V": 4.832612832387288, "C": 118.14253137734114, "stab": -2.2967549641927087}`. Includes layered (~86), olivine/fluorophosphate-family phosphates (~36 entries with C≈116-120), LiCrO2, Li-rich Li2MnO3, spinel-free list.  TAIL of file, verbatim (after the closing `]` of `points`):  ```json   "excluded": [     {       "na